course: dictionary
lesson: 15786
title: Ump, a short word from sports talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are short forms of longer words. Ump is short for umpire, the official who watches a game and decides if the rules are kept. «The ump waved his arm and shouted, "Strike!"» The waving and shouting show that the ump is in charge of the game.
explain: Sports fans often use short words like this when they talk about a game. Ella, who is from Canada, reads, «The ump called the runner out at first base.» She swaps in umpire: «The umpire called the runner out at first base.» It still makes sense, so ump must mean umpire.
explain: Context also tells you the tone of the speaker. «Kill the ump!» is a joking cry from angry fans in baseball. Nobody really wants harm to come to the umpire. The short word and the joke show that the speaker is a relaxed sports fan, not a referee or a coach.
fact: Ump is an informal, short word for umpire.
fact: Ump is mostly used in the US and Canada, especially in baseball.
fact: An umpire watches a game and decides if the rules are kept.
fact: In cricket and tennis, people more often say «umpire» in full, or «the umpie» in Australia.
fact: The plural of ump is umps, as in «Two umps stood behind the plate.»
exercise: «The ump called the runner out at first base.» What is an ump? | *A person who decides if the rules are kept in a game | A fan who shouts at the players | A player who runs around the bases | A type of ball used in baseball
exercise: Ump is a short word for which longer word? | Unicorn | *Umpire | Umbrella | Uniform
exercise: Jayden hears a crowd shout, «Kill the ump!» What does this joking cry show? | *Angry fans making a joke about the umpire | The game has ended and everyone is going home | The umpire has just won the game | The fans really want to hurt the umpire
test: Sam says, «The umpie waved his arm at the cricket ground.» Where do people most often say «the umpie»? | The United States | Scotland | *Australia | Canada
test: Which sentence uses ump correctly? | *«The ump said the batter was out.» | «The ump is a fruit that grows on trees.» | «The ump ran the bath for the dog.» | «The ump sang a song at the party.»
exam: What is the plural of ump? | *umps | umpers | umpies | ump's
</br>
